{
  "title": "Undifferentiated Pleomorphic Sarcoma",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8064/undifferentiated-pleomorphic-sarcoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 8 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Undifferentiated Pleomorphic Sarcoma, previously known as malignant fibrous histiocytoma, is a high-grade, aggressive, malignant fibrogenic tumor.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition is typically seen in patients 55-80 years of age who present with a slow-growing, painless mass.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a biopsy showing spindled, histiocytic, and multinucleated eosinophilic giant cells arranged in a storiform pattern arranged around small vessels.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually wide-margin surgical excision with radiotherapy.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
